1
00:00:10,156 --> 00:00:11,324
<i>Grandma, thanks to you,</i>

2
00:00:11,407 --> 00:00:14,994
I may be falling in love
for the first time!

3
00:00:15,954 --> 00:00:20,667
He doesn't need to put on a show.
I prefer him as he is.

4
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,127
You like him as he is?

5
00:00:23,211 --> 00:00:26,881
-Yay!
-Konta! Congratulations!

6
00:00:28,258 --> 00:00:30,218
-You did it!
-Thanks, Rinrin.

7
00:00:30,301 --> 00:00:31,511
Summer festival?

8
00:00:32,095 --> 00:00:33,346
Shall I guide you?

9
00:00:33,429 --> 00:00:35,140
Well, I'll go take a quick look.

10
00:00:35,223 --> 00:00:37,600
Hey, the two of them left together.

11
00:00:38,184 --> 00:00:41,104
<i>The fates of Grim Reapers</i>
<i>and humans do not cross.</i>

12
00:00:42,188 --> 00:00:46,067
<i>With death, their lives are fulfilled.</i>

13
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:03,084
Mr. Nishigami.

14
00:01:11,968 --> 00:01:14,137
Another hot day, huh?

15
00:01:16,014 --> 00:01:17,307
Yes.

16
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:29,360
I see.

17
00:01:29,444 --> 00:01:30,945
Orange peels…

18
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:32,864
How do you make them?

19
00:01:32,947 --> 00:01:34,866
They're surprisingly easy to make.

20
00:01:35,617 --> 00:01:37,535
If you want, we can make them together.

21
00:01:37,619 --> 00:01:38,995
No, I can't do it.

22
00:01:39,078 --> 00:01:40,371
You can!

23
00:01:40,455 --> 00:01:41,414
Here!

24
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:42,916
Here we go.

25
00:01:44,751 --> 00:01:46,920
What do I do with this?

26
00:01:47,003 --> 00:01:48,171
Huh? Oh, right.

27
00:01:49,672 --> 00:01:50,965
Put it on…

28
00:01:51,841 --> 00:01:52,675
There.

29
00:01:56,512 --> 00:01:58,932
Then, tie this in the front.

30
00:01:59,015 --> 00:02:00,141
All right.

31
00:02:02,435 --> 00:02:04,437
You two, your ice cream is going to melt.

32
00:02:05,146 --> 00:02:05,980
What?

33
00:02:07,857 --> 00:02:11,527
-Something's up…
-Maybe we shouldn't be here?

34
00:02:13,821 --> 00:02:15,782
Yo, Mr. Nishigami!

35
00:02:15,865 --> 00:02:17,533
That apron looks good on you.

36
00:02:18,159 --> 00:02:19,452
-Oh, Midori!
-Yes?

37
00:02:19,535 --> 00:02:21,287
Should I get some more beer?

38
00:02:21,371 --> 00:02:23,665
-Oh, please do. Thanks.
-Okay.

39
00:02:23,748 --> 00:02:26,292
Wait, Konta. I'm going with you. May I?

40
00:02:26,376 --> 00:02:27,377
Wait, really?

41
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:29,712
Oh, that's a big help. Let's go then!

42
00:02:29,796 --> 00:02:31,756
Yeah, let's go together.

43
00:02:32,757 --> 00:02:36,135
Oh, no. I'm the only one
without any summer romance!

44
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,139
Tetsuro!

45
00:02:40,223 --> 00:02:41,140
Yes?

46
00:02:41,683 --> 00:02:42,934
Going fishing?

47
00:02:43,017 --> 00:02:45,019
I'm going to fish for horse mackerel.

48
00:02:45,603 --> 00:02:46,938
Shall I come along with you?

49
00:02:48,022 --> 00:02:49,148
Sure.

50
00:02:49,232 --> 00:02:50,483
Let's hurry!

51
00:03:25,476 --> 00:03:27,061
-Butterfly.
-Butterfly!

52
00:03:27,562 --> 00:03:29,439
Hey, Konta, how did it go?

53
00:03:29,522 --> 00:03:31,691
The movie. <i>The Great Tenpo Famine</i>?

54
00:03:31,774 --> 00:03:33,776
Oh, they sent over the script.

55
00:03:35,945 --> 00:03:37,697
What are you grinning for?

56
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,283
Well, you see, I actually have lines.

57
00:03:40,366 --> 00:03:42,410
Seriously? That's amazing, Konta!

58
00:03:42,493 --> 00:03:44,329
Well, it's only one line, though.

59
00:03:46,622 --> 00:03:50,835
In order to survive,
you even have to eat grass!

60
00:03:51,544 --> 00:03:54,088
Wow, getting lines is amazing!

61
00:03:54,922 --> 00:03:57,008
It's all thanks to the documentary.

62
00:03:59,218 --> 00:04:01,179
All right, let's race to the sea.

63
00:04:01,262 --> 00:04:02,263
Ready, go!

64
00:04:02,347 --> 00:04:03,431
Hey, wait!

65
00:04:03,514 --> 00:04:05,058
I won't lose, okay?

66
00:04:06,142 --> 00:04:07,935
I'm not going to lose!

67
00:04:08,019 --> 00:04:08,978
Hey!

68
00:04:20,615 --> 00:04:23,451
Mr. Nishigami,
you are surprisingly clumsy.

69
00:04:24,077 --> 00:04:25,119
I'm sorry.

70
00:04:26,496 --> 00:04:29,874
I am not very used to this.

71
00:04:29,957 --> 00:04:31,125
It's okay.

72
00:04:31,209 --> 00:04:32,502
Just take it slow.

73
00:04:32,585 --> 00:04:34,379
Oh, watch your hands.

74
00:04:34,462 --> 00:04:35,671
Okay.

75
00:04:40,468 --> 00:04:41,594
What?

76
00:04:43,012 --> 00:04:44,180
This…

77
00:04:44,263 --> 00:04:45,807
is too thick!

78
00:04:45,890 --> 00:04:47,475
This is a wedge cut.

79
00:04:47,558 --> 00:04:48,851
It's hard to eat.

80
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:53,856
-I'm sorry. Then, I'll…
-Yes?

81
00:04:54,857 --> 00:04:56,025
What?

82
00:05:01,781 --> 00:05:02,824
So bitter.

83
00:05:18,548 --> 00:05:20,925
I've never done this before.

84
00:05:21,467 --> 00:05:22,885
Fishing is nice, huh.

85
00:05:24,303 --> 00:05:28,099
Just staring blankly at the sea
without thinking about anything.

86
00:05:28,182 --> 00:05:29,767
What a luxury.

87
00:05:30,685 --> 00:05:31,686
Yes.

88
00:05:32,728 --> 00:05:36,732
After coming here,
I've discovered how fun fishing is.

89
00:05:37,733 --> 00:05:41,988
I mean, it's certainly better than SNS.

90
00:05:43,823 --> 00:05:46,033
Oh, you mean social media.

91
00:05:46,117 --> 00:05:47,577
I don't use any.

92
00:05:49,745 --> 00:05:52,707
You know, my ex,

93
00:05:53,457 --> 00:05:56,669
he checks my social media quite a bit,

94
00:05:57,670 --> 00:05:59,630
and he leaves likes often.

95
00:06:01,007 --> 00:06:02,592
Oh, here it comes!

96
00:06:02,675 --> 00:06:06,762
-Here it comes!
-You got something! All right!

97
00:06:07,471 --> 00:06:09,140
Oh, wow!

98
00:06:09,223 --> 00:06:10,433
Wow!

99
00:06:10,516 --> 00:06:13,477
You got the first fish!

100
00:06:13,561 --> 00:06:14,687
Nice.

101
00:06:16,647 --> 00:06:18,441
And… posted.

102
00:06:18,524 --> 00:06:19,775
You're posting it?

103
00:06:20,818 --> 00:06:22,361
Oh! I did it without thinking!

104
00:06:22,445 --> 00:06:24,197
Yikes, I'm addicted.

105
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:27,200
But I'm glad it wasn't a total bust.

106
00:06:27,283 --> 00:06:28,701
Midori will be happy.

107
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:31,329
What? Bust?

108
00:06:31,412 --> 00:06:33,122
It's a fishing term.

109
00:06:33,206 --> 00:06:36,000
If you don't catch a single fish,
it's called a bust.

110
00:06:38,419 --> 00:06:39,795
But why Midori?

111
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:42,089
Oh, nothing.

112
00:06:42,173 --> 00:06:48,012
It's just that Midori likes cooking,
so I thought she would be happy.

113
00:06:48,095 --> 00:06:49,513
I see.

114
00:06:52,016 --> 00:06:53,309
All right.

115
00:06:53,392 --> 00:06:56,979
Let's catch a bunch
and have Midori make sashimi out of them.

116
00:06:57,063 --> 00:06:59,190
Let's buy some sake on the way back.

117
00:07:00,608 --> 00:07:03,152
-A sashimi party.
-Yeah!

118
00:07:03,236 --> 00:07:04,820
Party!

119
00:07:11,869 --> 00:07:13,871
Mr. Nishigami…

120
00:07:15,915 --> 00:07:18,251
Do you have a girlfriend?

121
00:07:20,253 --> 00:07:21,379
A girlfriend?

122
00:07:24,006 --> 00:07:25,132
No.

123
00:07:25,216 --> 00:07:28,219
I have no one like that.

124
00:07:30,429 --> 00:07:31,681
I see.

125
00:07:33,224 --> 00:07:36,561
Oh, by the way, I've never had one either.

126
00:07:36,644 --> 00:07:37,687
Surprising, right?

127
00:07:37,770 --> 00:07:39,564
I'm already 28.

128
00:07:39,647 --> 00:07:41,148
It's a red flag, isn't it?

129
00:07:42,191 --> 00:07:43,442
Is that so?

130
00:08:06,173 --> 00:08:07,592
Heave-ho.

131
00:08:08,217 --> 00:08:10,219
It's so windy today.

132
00:08:10,845 --> 00:08:12,013
Hup.

133
00:08:12,096 --> 00:08:13,889
-Rinrin!
-Yes?

134
00:08:14,473 --> 00:08:16,100
-What?
-I bought juice.

135
00:08:16,183 --> 00:08:18,060
-Huh? What kind of juice?
-Take a guess!

136
00:08:18,144 --> 00:08:19,770
What could it be? Coffee…

137
00:08:19,854 --> 00:08:21,188
-Coke.
-Oh, it's Coke.

138
00:08:21,272 --> 00:08:24,025
-You only got the "co" right.
-I did. Thank you.

139
00:08:24,108 --> 00:08:25,693
You were shaking it, right?

140
00:08:25,776 --> 00:08:27,653
-Did I? It will be fine.
-Will it?

141
00:08:28,446 --> 00:08:31,324
-No! What terrible luck!
-No!

142
00:08:31,407 --> 00:08:33,576
-It's all over me!
-Sorry, Rinrin!

143
00:08:39,999 --> 00:08:41,083
Hey, so…

144
00:08:41,834 --> 00:08:42,877
What?

145
00:08:44,837 --> 00:08:46,213
What exactly

146
00:08:47,923 --> 00:08:50,468
is our relationship right now?

147
00:08:52,511 --> 00:08:54,221
What kind of relationship…

148
00:08:55,348 --> 00:08:57,558
Well, about that…

149
00:08:58,184 --> 00:09:01,896
The other day, you know, during <i>Obon</i>,

150
00:09:02,813 --> 00:09:04,649
we, you know…

151
00:09:07,985 --> 00:09:09,070
Do you…

152
00:09:10,738 --> 00:09:12,698
think we can be a couple?

153
00:09:20,956 --> 00:09:26,337
"A woman's heart
is a deep ocean of secrets."

154
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:27,546
Hey!

155
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:30,424
Is that Rose's famous line from <i>Titanic</i>?

156
00:09:30,508 --> 00:09:33,177
Truly an actor!
You remembered it from just a line.

157
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:36,138
No, I love <i>Titanic</i>!
I remember lots of lines from it.

158
00:09:36,222 --> 00:09:37,932
So you watched the dubbed version?

159
00:09:38,015 --> 00:09:39,684
Well, of course. I don't know English.

160
00:09:42,895 --> 00:09:45,272
Between Rose and Jack,

161
00:09:45,356 --> 00:09:48,109
do you think the concept
of "dating" even existed?

162
00:09:48,192 --> 00:09:49,902
I don't know.

163
00:09:50,528 --> 00:09:52,238
They fell in love instantly,

164
00:09:52,321 --> 00:09:55,616
and before they could think about dating,
the ship went bam!

165
00:09:56,575 --> 00:10:02,665
Well, let's do fun things together,
then I'll think about us dating.

166
00:10:03,249 --> 00:10:05,042
Wait, so…

167
00:10:05,126 --> 00:10:06,752
I have a chance?

168
00:10:09,964 --> 00:10:12,591
All right, let's practice acting.

169
00:10:12,675 --> 00:10:13,718
-What?
-Oh!

170
00:10:13,801 --> 00:10:16,721
I want to play <i>Titanic </i>on that boat.

171
00:10:16,804 --> 00:10:18,222
Huh, on that fishing boat?

172
00:10:18,305 --> 00:10:19,849
-Yeah!
-Sure.

173
00:10:19,932 --> 00:10:21,642
-Really?
-Wait, Rinrin, your bag!

174
00:10:24,395 --> 00:10:28,149
-The sea is so vast and blue.
-Vast and blue!

175
00:10:28,983 --> 00:10:30,276
Konta!

176
00:10:30,359 --> 00:10:31,360
What, Rinrin?

177
00:10:31,444 --> 00:10:37,616
When you become famous and rich,
can you make me your stay-at-home wife?

178
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:38,826
What?

179
00:10:39,618 --> 00:10:42,246
Is this a proposal?

180
00:10:42,329 --> 00:10:48,127
If you become a popular actor,
I won't have to work anymore, right?

181
00:10:48,210 --> 00:10:51,881
I can just relax here
like this forever, right?

182
00:10:53,883 --> 00:10:55,176
All right.

183
00:10:55,259 --> 00:10:57,094
-Rinrin, here.
-Oh, okay.

184
00:10:57,178 --> 00:10:58,179
There you go.

185
00:11:03,142 --> 00:11:05,144
I will do my best!

186
00:11:06,687 --> 00:11:08,147
For you, Rinrin!

187
00:11:08,230 --> 00:11:10,733
I'll be the biggest star!

188
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,776
Good luck!

189
00:11:13,402 --> 00:11:14,737
Rinrin!

190
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:15,821
What?

191
00:11:15,905 --> 00:11:18,073
Can I say something
I like about you, Rinrin?

192
00:11:18,157 --> 00:11:19,241
Sure!

193
00:11:19,325 --> 00:11:20,868
Rinrin,

194
00:11:22,536 --> 00:11:23,996
your skin is so fair!

195
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,582
What are those two doing?

196
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:34,715
For some reason,

197
00:11:34,798 --> 00:11:39,261
when people stand in front of the sea,
they can't help but reenact <i>Titanic</i>.

198
00:11:40,429 --> 00:11:41,722
Huh? Who are you?

199
00:11:42,348 --> 00:11:43,599
How is it?

200
00:11:43,682 --> 00:11:45,726
Enjoying the life you have left?

201
00:11:45,809 --> 00:11:47,520
It's nice to be young.

202
00:11:47,603 --> 00:11:49,271
The life we have left?

203
00:11:49,355 --> 00:11:51,232
Yes, we're having fun…

204
00:11:51,315 --> 00:11:52,149
fishing.

205
00:11:52,691 --> 00:11:53,609
Oh, I see.

206
00:11:53,692 --> 00:11:55,528
Okay. That's a good thing.

207
00:11:55,611 --> 00:11:56,570
It's good.

208
00:11:56,654 --> 00:11:57,863
-Huh?
-It's good.

209
00:11:59,198 --> 00:12:00,950
It's nice to be young…

210
00:12:07,665 --> 00:12:12,253
Do you think she and Konta are dating?

211
00:12:12,336 --> 00:12:15,756
They kissed. It doesn't
necessarily mean they're dating.

212
00:12:15,839 --> 00:12:16,674
What?

213
00:12:17,216 --> 00:12:19,510
What do you mean by that?

214
00:12:21,845 --> 00:12:24,890
By the way,
you're interested in Midori, aren't you?

215
00:12:28,143 --> 00:12:29,186
What?

216
00:12:29,270 --> 00:12:31,021
Huh, wait?

217
00:12:31,105 --> 00:12:32,314
Am I?

218
00:12:33,399 --> 00:12:34,817
You don't even know?

219
00:12:35,609 --> 00:12:36,860
You like her, for sure.

220
00:12:36,944 --> 00:12:40,573
Look, you're even fishing for her sake.

221
00:12:41,991 --> 00:12:43,659
Midori is a good girl.

222
00:12:43,742 --> 00:12:45,995
She's a hard worker, and she's cute.

223
00:12:48,205 --> 00:12:50,082
I like her too.

224
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,085
But she probably…

225
00:13:02,761 --> 00:13:04,722
Sun-drying is nice, isn't it?

226
00:13:05,222 --> 00:13:09,101
They absorb a lot of sunlight,
so I'm sure they will turn out delicious.

227
00:13:09,893 --> 00:13:11,395
By drying them out like this,

228
00:13:12,479 --> 00:13:14,106
what will you achieve, in the end?

229
00:13:14,982 --> 00:13:17,943
I don't really understand it.

230
00:13:24,158 --> 00:13:25,909
I'm home!

231
00:13:25,993 --> 00:13:26,869
Welcome home.

232
00:13:27,453 --> 00:13:29,204
-Midori, look.
-What is it?

233
00:13:29,288 --> 00:13:30,623
-Midori.
-Hm?

234
00:13:30,706 --> 00:13:32,124
-We got a huge catch!
-What?

235
00:13:33,584 --> 00:13:35,044
Oh, wow!

236
00:13:35,127 --> 00:13:36,462
Now work your magic, Chef.

237
00:13:36,545 --> 00:13:38,255
I'm raring to go.

238
00:13:38,339 --> 00:13:39,298
I'll help too.

239
00:13:39,381 --> 00:13:41,258
-Okay.
-We've got to make sashimi.

240
00:13:41,342 --> 00:13:43,218
-Yeah!
-Sashimi!

241
00:13:43,302 --> 00:13:49,600
<i>Sashimi!</i>

242
00:13:49,683 --> 00:13:51,894
-What about fried?
-Sounds good too!

243
00:13:51,977 --> 00:13:54,688
<i>Fried!</i>

244
00:13:55,230 --> 00:13:56,357
Make <i>nanbanzuke</i>!

245
00:13:56,857 --> 00:13:59,526
<i>Nanbanzuke!</i>

246
00:14:00,444 --> 00:14:03,947
Tetsuro, bring out the plates.
Also, please chill the alcohol.

247
00:14:04,031 --> 00:14:05,074
Got it.

248
00:14:05,824 --> 00:14:07,743
As for you, Mr. Nishigami,

249
00:14:08,827 --> 00:14:12,915
can you cut some cucumber
to garnish the sashimi?

250
00:14:12,998 --> 00:14:15,250
-Here.
-Understood.

251
00:14:15,876 --> 00:14:18,921
Don't cut it too thick like earlier, okay?

252
00:14:19,713 --> 00:14:20,631
Yes.

253
00:14:21,507 --> 00:14:22,675
But…

254
00:14:22,758 --> 00:14:26,804
Cucumbers, even when thick,
are delicious, right?

255
00:14:26,887 --> 00:14:28,764
Well, true.

256
00:14:31,684 --> 00:14:34,561
-Look at this.
-What a nice photo!

257
00:14:34,645 --> 00:14:37,231
-Oh, I'm so embarrassed! My dimples!
-They're cute!

258
00:14:37,314 --> 00:14:39,858
-Dimples are so cute!
-I have one too.

259
00:14:39,942 --> 00:14:41,610
No, you don't.

260
00:14:41,694 --> 00:14:45,656
Somehow, this vacation
is making everyone lovey-dovey.

261
00:14:52,496 --> 00:14:56,125
Now then, put your hands together.

262
00:14:56,208 --> 00:14:57,710
Put your hands together.

263
00:14:58,502 --> 00:14:59,461
Let's eat.

264
00:14:59,545 --> 00:15:01,547
Let's eat!

265
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:03,632
-Tsumugi, pass the soy sauce.
-Okay.

266
00:15:03,716 --> 00:15:05,259
Tetsuro, shall I take this for you?

267
00:15:05,342 --> 00:15:07,302
-Thank you.
-Mr. Nishigami, here is the wasabi.

268
00:15:07,386 --> 00:15:09,847
-It looks good.
-Thank you.

269
00:15:09,930 --> 00:15:12,975
-All right, let's eat.
-Yum!

270
00:15:13,058 --> 00:15:16,103
When I remember that I caught these,
they taste twice as good.

271
00:15:16,812 --> 00:15:19,398
-Tsumugi caught two mackerels by herself.
-Really?

272
00:15:19,481 --> 00:15:22,109
-I might have a knack for fishing.
-Sure.

273
00:15:22,192 --> 00:15:26,405
By the way, Rinrin, Konta,
you two were reenacting <i>Titanic</i>, right?

274
00:15:26,488 --> 00:15:28,907
You were watching? How embarrassing.

275
00:15:28,991 --> 00:15:30,159
It's not embarrassing.

276
00:15:30,242 --> 00:15:33,078
In that moment,
we were totally Rose and Jack.

277
00:15:33,871 --> 00:15:35,122
What were you doing, Midori?

278
00:15:35,205 --> 00:15:38,792
I was making summer orange peels
with Mr. Nishigami, right?

279
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:40,878
I had fun.

280
00:15:41,462 --> 00:15:42,504
Me too.

281
00:15:45,049 --> 00:15:45,924
So good.

282
00:15:46,675 --> 00:15:47,509
Here.

283
00:15:50,262 --> 00:15:51,388
It's so nice.

284
00:15:51,472 --> 00:15:52,973
There's salad too.

285
00:15:53,057 --> 00:15:55,684
-Thank you.
-Here you go, the usual salad.

286
00:15:55,768 --> 00:15:57,728
Thanks for the salad.

287
00:15:59,229 --> 00:16:01,148
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

288
00:16:02,107 --> 00:16:03,942
Be careful on your way home.

289
00:16:04,026 --> 00:16:05,277
See you tomorrow.

290
00:16:06,570 --> 00:16:08,447
Yeah. See you tomorrow.

291
00:16:24,463 --> 00:16:25,464
AI.

292
00:16:25,547 --> 00:16:26,715
This is Tetsuro.

293
00:16:28,258 --> 00:16:31,720
Right now, I'm on vacation.

294
00:16:32,638 --> 00:16:35,265
And when I see a woman
I'm spending time with

295
00:16:36,183 --> 00:16:39,228
looking happy with another person,

296
00:16:40,521 --> 00:16:42,397
another man…

297
00:16:44,483 --> 00:16:46,819
my chest tightens.

298
00:16:49,029 --> 00:16:51,532
And before I know it, I…

299
00:16:52,199 --> 00:16:54,701
I find myself thinking only about her.

300
00:16:56,578 --> 00:16:59,456
What is this feeling?

301
00:17:01,041 --> 00:17:02,334
<i>Tetsuro.</i>

302
00:17:03,585 --> 00:17:07,673
<i>That feeling of yours is most likely love.</i>

303
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:09,383
Love?

304
00:17:10,175 --> 00:17:12,928
<i>By the way, you mentioned</i>
<i>you are on vacation.</i>

305
00:17:13,011 --> 00:17:16,223
<i>When humans are placed</i>
<i>in an unusual environment,</i>

306
00:17:16,306 --> 00:17:19,143
<i>they develop romantic feelings</i>
<i>more easily.</i>

307
00:17:20,394 --> 00:17:24,439
<i>Since AIs do not have emotions,</i>
<i>we cannot experience love or jealousy.</i>

308
00:17:24,523 --> 00:17:26,316
<i>We don't have vacations either.</i>

309
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,694
<i>Vacations are a human privilege.</i>

310
00:17:29,903 --> 00:17:31,530
A human privilege?

311
00:17:32,406 --> 00:17:36,618
On vacation, people fall in love.
It's like a principle.

312
00:17:40,038 --> 00:17:41,373
A vacation

313
00:17:42,583 --> 00:17:43,709
principle?

314
00:17:52,259 --> 00:17:53,510
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

315
00:17:54,303 --> 00:17:57,890
<i>Your recent actions</i>
<i>have been unacceptable.</i>

316
00:17:57,973 --> 00:18:00,225
<i>Do you understand what I mean?</i>

317
00:18:02,895 --> 00:18:04,062
I'm not sure.

318
00:18:04,813 --> 00:18:06,064
<i>Back during </i>Obon<i>,</i>

319
00:18:06,148 --> 00:18:09,610
<i>I was relieved that you understood</i>
<i>your position as a Grim Reaper,</i>

320
00:18:09,693 --> 00:18:13,280
<i>but now you're getting</i>
<i>friendly again with those people.</i>

321
00:18:14,114 --> 00:18:16,283
<i>The Sea God reported to me as much.</i>

322
00:18:16,366 --> 00:18:17,910
<i>What's wrong, Grim Reaper?</i>

323
00:18:17,993 --> 00:18:19,161
<i>Surely…</i>

324
00:18:19,244 --> 00:18:22,164
<i>You haven't forgotten</i>
<i>your mission, have you?</i>

325
00:18:27,336 --> 00:18:30,547
There is no way I would do such a thing.

326
00:18:30,631 --> 00:18:33,008
<i>Then why are you being their friend?</i>

327
00:18:37,596 --> 00:18:39,806
<i>As a Grim Reaper,</i>

328
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:42,935
<i>there is no need for you</i>
<i>to have bonds with humans.</i>

329
00:18:43,018 --> 00:18:45,145
<i>Furthermore, given your position,</i>

330
00:18:45,229 --> 00:18:48,565
<i>falling in love with a human</i>
<i>is out of the question.</i>

331
00:18:48,649 --> 00:18:50,025
<i>Do you understand?</i>

332
00:18:52,361 --> 00:18:53,862
I do.

333
00:18:55,030 --> 00:18:56,740
<i>A typhoon is coming soon.</i>

334
00:18:57,449 --> 00:19:01,495
<i>Because of it, a landslide will occur,</i>
<i>and that villa will be destroyed.</i>

335
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:05,999
<i>Those five you are</i>
<i>so close with will all die.</i>

336
00:19:07,125 --> 00:19:11,672
<i>Witnessing their demise</i>
<i>is your duty as a Grim Reaper.</i>

337
00:19:12,422 --> 00:19:14,424
<i>Don't forget that.</i>

338
00:19:17,803 --> 00:19:19,554
Be careful on your way home.

339
00:19:19,638 --> 00:19:20,597
See you tomorrow.

340
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:48,250
<i>It's finally here.</i>

341
00:19:48,333 --> 00:19:50,294
<i>Midori's first love.</i>

342
00:19:50,377 --> 00:19:52,713
Hey, Midori, seriously?

343
00:19:52,796 --> 00:19:55,424
<i>Mr. Nishigami hasn't come</i>
<i>for the past two days.</i>

344
00:19:55,507 --> 00:19:57,467
He isn't playing
with Midori's feelings, right?

345
00:19:57,551 --> 00:19:58,593
Mr. Nishigami…

346
00:19:58,677 --> 00:20:00,929
You said, "See you tomorrow"…

347
00:20:01,013 --> 00:20:05,267
Because of this vacation,
it's now easier for us to fall in love.

348
00:20:05,350 --> 00:20:07,102
Why not make a move on Midori?

349
00:20:07,185 --> 00:20:08,270
<i>I…</i>

350
00:20:08,353 --> 00:20:09,730
Mr. Nishigami…

351
00:20:10,355 --> 00:20:11,648
<i>I'm the one at fault here.</i>

352
00:20:11,732 --> 00:20:12,816
Seriously?

353
00:20:12,899 --> 00:20:14,109
What is that supposed to mean?

354
00:20:14,192 --> 00:20:15,944
So it was all my misunderstanding?

355
00:20:16,611 --> 00:20:18,488
<i>Mr. Nishigami, could it be…</i>

356
00:20:19,156 --> 00:20:20,782
<i>you have come to dislike us?</i>

357
00:20:21,616 --> 00:20:22,576
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

